<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Var (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Var is a river of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> that flows about 114 kilometres from the Maritime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> just west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a>. In antiquity it formed the boundary between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and until 1860 its lower course marked the border between France and the County of Nice, ruled by Savoy. It gave its name to the Var <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, through which it no longer flows since the boundary changes of 1860.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/var-river.jpg" alt="Var (river)" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrevaux-rooftops.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
